 *Q1. What is Exception? Write a program for exception handling*

*Answer:* 
An exception is an event that interrupts the normal flow of a program when an error or unexpected situation occurs. Instead of the program continuing normally, an exception is "thrown" so it can be handled.

*Java Example:*
public class ExceptionDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            int a = 10;
            int b = 0;
            int result = a / b;  // Ithu la ArithmeticException varum
            System.out.println("Result: " + result);
        } 
        catch (ArithmeticException e) {
            System.out.println("Error: Cannot divide by zero!");
        } 
        finally {
            System.out.println("This will always execute");
        }
    }
}
*Output:*
Error: Cannot divide by zero!
This will always execute
*Python Example:*
try:
    a = 10
    b = 0
    result = a / b  # ZeroDivisionError
    print("Result:", result)
